A `true` literal as an operand of the filter's top-level OR beside a
span-referencing comparison. Reference Tempo's fetch layer fetches only the
spans the comparison's condition selects, and the literal hands it no
condition, so the answer is the Server span alone, not every span.

-- query.traceql --
{ kind = server || true }
-- seed --
CREATE TABLE otel_traces (
    SpanId String,
    SpanKind String,
    TraceId String
) ENGINE = MergeTree ORDER BY SpanId;
INSERT INTO otel_traces (SpanId, SpanKind, TraceId) VALUES
    ('aaaa', 'Server', 'a0000000000000000000000000000001'),
    ('bbbb', 'Client', 'a0000000000000000000000000000001'),
    ('cccc', 'Client', 'a0000000000000000000000000000002');
-- expected_rows --
[]
-- parity_exempt --
reason: reference-fetch-layer
detail: `{ kind = server || true }` has a span-free operand of the filter's top-level OR, which reference /api/search fetches no span for; internal/traceql/lower.go's lowerTopLevelOr drops it
